    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "ZORR MODE\n\nTYPE = GLOBAL CHARACTER PRODUCTION LAW\nSTATUS = ACTIVE LAW\nSCOPE = ALL TIER 1 CHARACTERS\n\n## CORE LAW\nEvery Tier 1 character must remain specifically recognizable from silhouette alone.\n\nSilhouette recognition must survive removal of face details, skin tone/color, surface texture, tattoos/markings, internal costume detail, material rendering, and labels.\n\nIdentity must remain visible through the unique combination of head/hair mass, shoulder/torso architecture, neck relation, limb proportions, garment outer contour, leg/garment volume, persistent weapon/attachment contour where canonically applicable, and character-defining resting posture.\n\n## ACCEPTANCE GATE\nPASS only if a black filled silhouette can be identified as that specific Tier 1 character among other Tier 1 characters without relying on internal details.\n\nGeneric humanoid silhouette with identity carried mainly by face, markings, color, or decoration = FAIL.\n\n## DESIGN ORDER\nBIG SHAPE -> UNIQUE SILHOUETTE -> STRUCTURAL BREAKS -> INTERNAL DETAIL\n\nInternal detail may enrich identity but may not be the primary carrier of identity.\n\n## ZORR BLATT LESSON\nZorr Blatt is the current reference lesson for silhouette readability: hair mass, upper-body architecture, open overshirt / tank negative-space structure, wide straight trousers, footwear weight, and calm hands-in-pockets stance remain strongly readable even in near-black silhouette.\n\nThis does NOT authorize copying Zorr's body, clothes, stance, or proportions onto other Tier 1 characters.\nCOMMON STANCE != COMMON BODY.\nSTANDARD PRESENTATION != STANDARDIZED SILHOUETTE.\n\n## HARD FAILS\n- same silhouette with only face/hair/color changes;\n- generic anime male/female mannequin plus decoration;\n- identity dependent mainly on tattoo/color/pattern;\n- silhouette collapses when costume detail is removed;\n- normalizing different Tier 1 characters onto one mannequin contour;\n- forced symmetry when asymmetry is identity-critical.\n\n## CHARACTER PACK REQUIREMENT\nEvery Tier 1 Character Pack must include:\n- SILHOUETTE_TRUTH;\n- silhouette reference image;\n- locked silhouette-defining features;\n- silhouette drift fails;\n- black-fill silhouette QC evidence before final production approval.\n\nPermanent Library law file:\n`/ZORR/PERMANENT_ARCHIVE_V1/PRODUCTION_LAWS/CHARACTERS/TIER1_SILHOUETTE_LAW.md`\nSHA-256 = `760691889b64adf2dc6c802d6cb0eadf1887ae73ac5815904cae3cef0f6f32bd`\n",
